From 67208cd723695d62faf4b1cb278964703274c617 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:49:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] The Inner Garden, Phase 1 polish: honest adds, her
 profile first, a fuller entrance

Fixes from the engineering, phone and brand reviews:

- The rooms wait for her profile row as well as her sign-in (2.5 s at most),
  so a member who gave her birthday is never asked again, and a bud never
  turns into her stone mid-entrance. The bloom on Your stone now plays only
  for a birthday saved there, scrolled into view, with the card rising after.
- addToBag reports whether the shop took the piece; the card says "In your
  bag." only then and is ready to try again otherwise. A month the listing
  does not carry says so, with no price and no "Sold out".
- The card names the variant as its colour and the stone in the listing's
  words (heart-cut cubic zirconia). The Gate promises only rooms that exist.
- The Doors: the flower draws large with a cream under-line, glints, drops
  into the latch, and the gates (solid until the last of the swing) open as
  the curtain lifts onto the garden; petals fall onto it after the Doors go.
  Everything is built at mount and starts once the page settles; the garden
  blooms in by band (12 animations, not ~75). Greeting in ink on sage.
- Her stone flower holds the heart-cut stone at its centre, and its head
  now sits on top of its stem (a nested-svg sizing bug had dropped it).
  Taps on her own two flowers answer specially; one bloom teaches the tap.
  Tap blooms animate their inner whorl on its own compositor layer.
- Clarity masks every signed-in screen; the preview needs localhost too.
  Gate CTA on the first screen; larger, darker small type.

The global CSS and vendor chunk stay byte-identical to origin/main.

